{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:25:49.553Z","data":{"text":"`change_folder_seal` is in place, and every archived seal matches its marker except exactly 002 to 016 and 018 to 027. The task `verify` passes (5 tests in `reading_seal`, 1 corpus test in `seal_corpus`), and `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` passes. The mutants step in that script did not run because `OSQ_DIFF` is not set, so there is no mutation check on `seal.rs`.\n\n- **Fixtures:** I copied the seal fixtures and `seals.json` byte for byte into `crates/kernel/storage/tests/`. I did not check that `undecodable/bytes.bin` and `undecodable/bom.md` kept their bytes, but the `undecodable` seal matches the golden one.\n- **Walk:** It uses `DirEntry::file_type`, so symbolic links are not followed or read. It skips `.run`, `.git` and `.DS_Store` at any depth, and `plan-prompt.md` at the root only. Read failures come back as `StorageError::Read` naming the path.\n- **Wiring:** `read/mod.rs` declares the module and adds its `Implements:` line, and `lib.rs` re-exports `change_folder_seal`.\n- **Tests:** The symlink case is its own `#[cfg(unix)]` test, apart from the loop over the other added paths.\n\nThe result file is at `openspec/changes/223-rust-approval-seal/.run/results/2.md`."}}
